{"entryId":"3164","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3164:1","sourceSha256":"e279813a4b05ba13d61b1465b6793c8b24769c7128d8e989e05e7a96d9e2e1c1","englishSha256":"828c16c8783c63d4a195f2547a06b441e4c2e48d8a7defd6904d3f5c78ad3668","citations":[{"id":"3164:1:link-001","he":[26,212],"en":[69,81],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_136a.16"},"reference":"Shabbat 136a:16","assessment":"The Bavli gives just “the son of Rav Idi bar Avin” and spells the idiom עיגלא תילתא. Tosafot explicitly use the calf’s seventh day to reject the third-grown interpretation and prefer a fine calf, with another view third-born. The timing and guests remain.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 136a:16","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_136a.16"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Tosafot on Gittin 56a:3:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Gittin_56a.3.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3164:1:link-002","he":[26,212],"en":[46,67],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Gittin_56a.3.1"},"reference":"Tosafot on Gittin 56a:3:1","assessment":"The Bavli gives just “the son of Rav Idi bar Avin” and spells the idiom עיגלא תילתא. Tosafot explicitly use the calf’s seventh day to reject the third-grown interpretation and prefer a fine calf, with another view third-born. The timing and guests remain.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Gittin 56a:3:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Gittin_56a.3.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Shabbat 136a:16","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_136a.16"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3164:1:link-003","he":[214,238],"en":[322,362],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Shabbat_19.7.1"},"reference":"Rosh on Shabbat 19:7:1","assessment":"Exact reading in the Rosh; the Bavli leaves the son unnamed. Preserve both views.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rosh on Shabbat 19:7:1